        <item>
            <title>0.8.11</title>
            <pubDate>Thu, 06 Aug 2026 19:52:43 +0700</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>0.8.11</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.8.11</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>What's new in 0.8.11</h2>
<ul>
<li>Folder arrange, finished: dragging a pill now shows exactly where it will land — one blue target for a single pill, two for a linked couple (it takes both seats) — and the pills that have to move step aside while you drag, so releasing changes nothing you haven&#x27;t already seen</li>
<li>Linked couples travel as one slice and can&#x27;t be split by a drag or have half of them evicted; open (unlinked) pairs move independently — drag a main onto a main and only the mains swap</li>
<li>Both layers now animate identically: outer (⌥) pills travel on the same glide as the mains instead of springing into place</li>
<li>Undo and redo in arrange mode: ⌘Z / ⇧⌘Z, plus buttons above the ring</li>
<li>Deleting a pill in arrange asks first, and deleted pills are kept in the Pill Library&#x27;s History</li>
<li>Pill Library at the top-right of arrange mode: your saved pills, deleted pills, and a suggestion made from whatever link you last copied — drag any of them straight into a slot</li>
<li>Edits apply immediately: changing a pill&#x27;s safeguard, label or colour now takes effect without closing and reopening the menu</li>
<li>A pad tap can&#x27;t switch menus while you&#x27;re dragging in arrange</li>
<li>The menu-bar volume slider uses the full width of the menu</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
